WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
After Emperor Xuanzong ascended the throne, he governed with great diligence and opened a whole new era.

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:11.126
Every day he worked diligently on state affairs and listened carefully to his ministers' advice.

00:00:11.476 --> 00:00:17.740
Merchants and travelers gathered in the capital Chang'an; it was lively beyond compare and the economy was thriving.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:23.034
Merchants from faraway lands brought many precious goods.

00:00:23.384 --> 00:00:29.504
The fields gave rich harvests, the granaries were full, and the people lived and worked in peace and contentment.

00:00:29.854 --> 00:00:35.854
Poetry, music and dance flourished, and culture reached an unprecedented height.

00:00:36.204 --> 00:00:41.724
Great poets such as Li Bai and Du Fu also lived in this age.

00:00:42.074 --> 00:00:47.858
Envoys from many countries came to Chang'an one after another, and the prestige of the Great Tang spread far in all directions.

00:00:48.208 --> 00:00:54.472
This period is known as the Kaiyuan Prosperity, the most glorious age of the flourishing Tang.

00:00:54.822 --> 00:01:00.462
People still fondly remember that glorious golden age today.

